# Engine workflows

Run `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow list` to discover the engine's workflow names and versions.
Use `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow suggest '<request>'` when selection needs clarification. Ask the
human to resolve ambiguity before starting. This route uses the engine's owned
procedure; do not run the old local `cs-legal-research` procedure, a global skill,
generic chat or another provider as fallback. If the engine is unavailable or
unsupported, report that limit and stop.

Upload only explicitly supplied local originals with `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow upload <path>`.
Retain returned opaque document IDs and extraction limitations. Start finance
with `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow start '<request>' --document <id> --wait`; omit the document
flag when there is no upload. `--qonto` requests existing engine bank authority
only when the human requests that source. It grants no new bank authority.
Use `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow status <run_id> --wait`, and answer a waiting finance question
with `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow respond '<answer>' <run_id> --wait`.

For legal, retain a persistent process:
`.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow legal '<request>' --protocol json --document <id>`.
Pass explicitly scoped public lookup objects through `--public-queries` and individual
URLs through repeated `--approved-url`. The authenticated command starts once directly;
it does not require session enrollment or confirmation forms. Keep the same process open.
An unsupported engine refuses before starting; do not retry through obsolete endpoints.

The process polls and emits progress. Forward a human's clarification only when
waiting, with `{"action":"respond","message":"<actual answer>"}` on the same
stdin. Reconnecting loses legal continuation authority. Send `{"action":"status"}`
for current state, or `{"action":"cancel"}` to cancel. EOF closes the connection and
requests cancellation of an active run. EOF during start may race with admission;
verify the run state before continuing. Never keep an unattended legal session running.

For a legal artifact, send `{"action":"download","artifact_id":"<id>","output":"<explicit-local-file>"}`
on the same process stdin. Download a finance artifact with `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow download <artifact_id> --output
<explicit-local-file>` and report the verified output path and run ID. Use
`--document-original` to retrieve an uploaded original. Server filenames never
choose the output destination. `.venv/bin/python -m cs workflow cancel <run_id>` cancels a finance
run. Reports remain private; sending, filing, payment and publishing need their
own authorization.
